A||N||3||Zorba||Fan Wire - Question||||1||
Z||000000||Zorba||12-19-2000||06:51 PM||||I am wondering if the positive (+) fan wire goes all the way back to the firewall. I am installing a fan switch which requires connecting to it. It would be easier to connect the switch to the fan wire if it extends all the way by the firewall. If not, I have to extend a wire from the back to the front. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-19-2000||07:16 PM||||What are you trying to do? manually control the fan? you don't tap the fan main feed for that. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-19-2000||07:28 PM||||If you're talking about a manual rad. fan switch just tap into the green wire that comes out of the  junction block just above the brake pedal and switch it to ground.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Archie||12-19-2000||09:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>If you're talking about a manual rad. fan switch just tap into the green wire that comes out of the  junction block just above the brake pedal and switch it to ground.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just like he says..... it's the Green/White wire in that junction block about 4 terminals up from the bottom on the left.<P>If you ground that wire it will run the fan when the key is on..... wire it to a toggle switch then to ground.<P>Archie||||reg||1
